---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const values = [
  { name: 'Humility > Pride', body: 'The Lord promises to bless the one &ldquo;who is humble and contrite in spirit&rdquo; (Isaiah 66:2). Humility is simply an accurate view of God and of ourselves. It is the foundation of every other virtue &mdash; without it, we have neither the desire nor the grace to grow. The gospel itself humbles us: &ldquo;By grace you have been saved through faith. And this is not your own doing; it is the gift of God, not a result of works, so that no one may boast&rdquo; (Ephesians 2:8&ndash;9). No one stands tall at the foot of the cross.' },
  { name: 'Courage > Cowardice', body: 'God expects his people to be courageous (Deuteronomy 31:6; Philippians 1:28). Counterintuitively, courage flows from humility, and cowardice from pride. The proud man has too much to lose. The humble man has already lost it all and been given everything back in Christ. We want to help people live genuinely courageous lives as an expression of humble trust in the God who has promised never to leave them nor forsake them.' },
  { name: 'Celebration > Envy', body: "Scripture treats envy as a far more serious problem than most people realize. It sits at the root of many evils, ancient and modern &mdash; from the first murder to the crucifixion itself, which Pilate knew was driven by envy (Mark 15:10). But in the cross, Jesus made it possible to genuinely root for one another and to celebrate each other's successes as our own. You would be surprised how different a community becomes when envy is named and rejected." },
  { name: 'Facts > Feelings', body: 'Feelings matter a great deal &mdash; God made us to feel deeply, and Scripture is full of commanded emotion. But feelings make poor governors. When our feelings and the facts disagree, we work to bring our feelings into line with the truth, not the other way around. This is not stoicism. It is sanity.' },
  { name: 'Honesty > Spin', body: "We try to say what we mean and mean what we say. &ldquo;We have renounced disgraceful, underhanded ways. We refuse to practice cunning or to tamper with God's word, but by the open statement of the truth we would commend ourselves to everyone's conscience in the sight of God&rdquo; (2 Corinthians 4:2). Plain speech is a form of love." },
  { name: 'Freedom > Guilt', body: 'The world, following its father the devil, uses guilt to bully people into conformity. Christ does something entirely different: he deals with guilt rather than weaponizing it. We have been set free, and we actually believe what we confess &mdash; that &ldquo;if we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness&rdquo; (1 John 1:9). A church built on forgiven people has no use for shame as a management tool.' },
];
---
<Base
  title="About | Providence Community Church | Church in Lenexa, KS."
  description="Learn more about the mission, partnerships, and core values that act as a foundation for Providence Community Church."
  path="/about/"
>
  <section class="section section-panel">
    <div class="wrap grid-2">
      <div>
        <h1 style="font-family:var(--serif); font-weight:400; font-size:1.8rem; line-height:1.4;">We are called to display truth and beauty in community.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="photo">
        <img src="/wp-content/uploads/Providence_About_FirePit.jpg" alt="Gathering around the fire pit at Providence" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Things we value.</h2>
      <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:36px; gap:36px;">
        {values.map((v) => (
          <div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;">{v.name}</h3>
            <p style="font-size:0.95rem;">{v.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule section-panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Partnerships</p>
      <h2 style="max-width:30ch;">United in fellowship, mission, and governance.</h2>
      <p style="max-width:62ch;">We enjoy a rich relationship with Sovereign Grace Churches worldwide, a family of churches that helps us to care for one another and advance the gospel.</p>
      <div style="display:flex; gap:48px; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:24px;">
        <a href="https://www.sovereigngrace.com/" style="display:block; max-width:240px;">
          <img src="/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/SGC-1024x343.png" alt="Sovereign Grace Churches — united in fellowship, mission, and governance" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:18px;"><a class="arrow-link" href="https://www.sovereigngrace.com/">Visit Sovereign Grace Churches</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore Providence</p>
      <h2>What's your next step?</h2>
      <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:36px;">
        <div>
          <h3>Read our beliefs</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.95rem;">What we believe about the Bible instructs everything that we value as a church.</p>
          <a class="arrow-link" href="/beliefs/">Our beliefs</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Get connected</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.95rem;">Discover the ways you can connect and grow here at Providence.</p>
          <a class="arrow-link" href="/community/">Community</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Plan your visit</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.95rem;">Take the next step by learning what you can expect on a Sunday morning.</p>
          <a class="arrow-link" href="/visit/">Visit on Sunday</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
